   "headline": "Knicks hold off Raptors 122-120 to end preseason",
   "story": "New York led 35-32 after the first quarter and 63-58 at halftime, and its largest lead was 10 points, at 47-37 in the second quarter. Toronto's largest lead was 6, at 15-9 in the first. The Knicks led 87-79 going into the fourth, but the Raptors outscored them 41-35 in that quarter and tied it at 117-117 with 1:03 left. Karl-Anthony Towns had 13 points, 15 rebounds and 9 assists for New York, Jalen Brunson scored 20, and Scottie Barnes had 23 points and 4 blocks for Toronto.",
